## Stop .gitignore from dropping digitaltwin.build at deploy
================================================================================

Context:
The 0.9.0 app crashed on start with ``ModuleNotFoundError: No module named
'back.objects.digitaltwin.build'``. DAB applies ``.gitignore``; the recursive
``build/`` pattern matched ``src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/`` and omitted
TwinGraphBuild from the Apps workspace even though the files are in git.

Changes:

1. .gitignore
   Anchor packaging artifacts as ``/build/`` and ``/dist/`` (repo root only).
2. .databricksignore
   Same root-only ``/build/`` / ``/dist/`` with a comment matching the
   ``internal/`` warning.
3. tests/units/api/test_help_api.py
   Guard that ``.gitignore`` does not use a bare ``build/`` and that the
   package ``__init__.py`` is tracked.

