## OWL generation: percent-encode invalid IRIs instead of failing
================================================================================

Context:
GitHub Sync all reported "OWL generation failed" for cafds/V1 and wrfmshell/V2.
Their stored URIs contain spaces (".../cafds#Affected asset", base URI
".../WRFM - Shell#"). rdflib refuses to serialize those as Turtle, so the OWL
view/export and the mirrored <Domain>.owl.ttl failed for such domains.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/w3c/owl/iri.py (new)
   escape_iri() percent-encodes the characters RFC 3987 forbids in an IRI
   (whitespace, <>"{}|\^`). Valid and non-ASCII IRIs are left as they are.
   serialize_turtle() serializes a graph as Turtle and rebuilds it with
   escaped IRIs (terms and namespace bindings) only when needed, logging a
   warning.
2. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py
   generate() serializes through serialize_turtle() (no class growth).
3. tests/units/ontology/test_owl_iri_escaping.py (new)
   escape_iri cases, unchanged output for valid graphs, and generator output
   with spaces in base and entity URIs that parses back.
4. docs/sphinx/api/app.core.w3c.rst
   Document the iri module.

Modified files:
- src/back/core/w3c/owl/iri.py
- src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py
