## Navbar Save: spinner while the domain is being saved
================================================================================

Context:
The top-right "Save" button gave no visual feedback during a registry save,
apart from a transient toast, and could be clicked again mid-save.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/global/js/navbar.js
   New setDomainSaveBusy(): hides the Save icon, shows a small spinner, sets
   aria-busy and an is-saving state. domainSave() validates first, turns the
   busy state on, and always restores it in finally. A re-entrancy guard
   ignores extra clicks / Ctrl+S during a save.
2. src/front/static/global/css/main.css
   .ob-subnav-save-btn.is-saving (no pointer events, progress cursor) and
   .ob-save-spinner sizing to match the icon. The existing .disabled fade is
   left untouched.

